                <pb facs="0235" n="151" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg151"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1903</hi></date>.
                        (Received 6.10 p.m., June 25.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>June 17, 4 p.m. Members of Congress arriving. Opposition to the ratifications of
                    the canal convention is very strong. Public opinion is that the convention will
                    not be ratified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
